! TDDFT mode matrix 02/16 -- TDHF / RPA  (HF reference, no TDA)
!
! Same reference as case 01 but the full non-Hermitian Casida problem
! (A+B)(A-B) instead of A alone.  Every RPA excitation energy must lie
! BELOW its TDA partner in case 01 -- the de-excitation block can only
! lower the eigenvalues.  That inequality is the physics check here.
%method  HF
%basis   sto-3g
%job     energy
%charge  0
%mult    1
%tddft   3
%tddft_tda off
%tddft_multiplicity singlet
%geom angstrom
O    0.000000    0.000000    0.117300
H    0.000000    0.757200   -0.469200
H    0.000000   -0.757200   -0.469200
*end
